   width instead of the 1071 px grid extent, so the grid produced 5 columns and
   the test caught it. Constant and comment now carry the real derivation.
2. The narrower tile exposed a genuine 22 px RenderFlex overflow in the
   PosterCard metadata row, caught by movies_screen_test.dart. The year now
   absorbs slack via Expanded and the quality badge is capped at 72 px.

Why: the owner reported that roughly three large posters fit in one row and
that browsing movies was very hard. Two full rows cannot fit in the old 407 px
grid viewport at any comfortable poster size, so the vertical space had to come
from Continue Watching (213 of 720 logical px), which the owner accepted moving
to Home only.

